@* The EPA an activity is evidence for, as a list cell (T137). "Code — Title", the form every other EPA surface uses;
   a dash when the activity is about no EPA.

   T231. An EPA that is not in force now is marked "(no longer in use)": the words the activity's own EPA picker uses
   (EpaOptionLabel, D48), for the same EPA, because the flag is the one that picker reads (Epa.IsActive, carried as
   ActivitySummaryDto.EpaInForce). The text and the mark are the shared EpaLabel's (T255), which the trajectory headings
   and the entrustment decision lists use too. *@
@if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Code))
{
  <span>—</span>
}
else
{
  <span><EpaLabel Code="@Code" Title="@Title" InForce="@(InForce != false)" /></span>
}

@code {
  [Parameter] public string? Code { get; set; }
  [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }

  /// <summary>
  /// Whether the EPA is in force now (<see cref="ActivitySummaryDto.EpaInForce" />), or null when there is no EPA.
  /// Required, so a list that shows an activity's EPA cannot leave out that it is no longer in use.
  /// </summary>
  [Parameter, EditorRequired] public bool? InForce { get; set; }
}
